{"cuisine/cuisine-of-liguria":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/cuisine-of-liguria","n":"Ligurian cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Italy","intro":[["Ligurian cuisine consists of dishes from the culinary tradition of Liguria, a region of northwestern Italy, which makes use of ingredients linked both to local production (such as preboggion, a mixture of wild herbs), and to imports from areas with which, over the centuries, the Ligurians have had frequent trade (such as Sardinian pecorino, one of the ingredients of pesto)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"cuisine-of-liguria"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuisine_of_Liguria"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"A Small Kitchen in Genoa","ref":"site/asmallkitcheningenoa-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"asmallkitcheningenoa.com","note":"Genoese cook Enrica Monzani's English-language blog of Ligurian recipes.","url":"https://asmallkitcheningenoa.com/about","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Liguria: The Cookbook","ref":"cookbook/liguria-the-cookbook","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Laurel Evans","note":"Recipes from the Italian Riviera by a Liguria-based American writer, published by Rizzoli.","url":"https://rizzoliusa.com/book/9780847870615","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":2,"links":[["Baxin","dish/baxin"],["Coniglio alla sanremese","dish/coniglio-alla-sanremese"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Fennel","ingredient/fennel"],["Lemon","ingredient/lemon"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Rabbit meat","ingredient/rabbit-meat"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/9/9a/Baxin.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imagein