, Greek oregano, and olive oil. Common additions include lemon juice, green bell pepper, caper berries (especially on the Cyclades islands), and mint or parsley for decoration (mainly in Northern Greece). Greek salad is often imagined as a farmer's breakfast or lunch, as its ingredients resemble those that a Greek farmer might have on hand."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-greek-salad"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greek_salad"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":9,"links":[["Cucumber","ingredient/cucumber"],["Edible salt","ingredient/edible-salt"],["Feta","ingredient/feta"],["Kalamata olive","ingredient/kalamata-olive"],["Olive","ingredient/olive"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Oregano","ingredient/oregano"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Dimitra's Dishes","ref":"site/dimitrasdishes-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dimitrasdishes.com","note":"Dimitra Alfieris's video channel and blog focused on classic Greek home cooking.","url":"https://dimitrasdishes.com","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Greek cuisine","links":[["Alexis Restaurant","dish/alexis-restaurant"],["Avgolemono","dish/avgolemono"],["Baba ghanoush","dish/baba-ghanoush"],["Bouyiourdi","dish/bouyiourdi"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Dametra Cafe","dish/dametra-cafe"],["Diples","dish/diples"],["Fasolada","dish/fasolada"],["Freddo cappuccino","dish/freddo-cappuccino"],["Greek restaurant","dish/greek-restaurant"],["İmam bayıldı","dish/imam-bay-ld"],["Kakavia (soup)","dish/kakavia-soup"],["Kalitsounia","dish/kalitsounia"],["Karydopita","dish/karydopita"],["Keşkek","dish/keskek"],["Ladera","dish/ladera"],["Noumboulo","dish/noumboulo"],["Pithari Taverna","dish/pithari-taverna"],["Psarosoupa","dish/psarosoupa"],["Spanakorizo","dish/spanakorizo"],["Taramasalata","dish/taramasalata"],["Tzatziki","dish/tzatziki"],["Yia Yia Mary's","dish/yia-yia-mary-s"]]}]},"dish/mongolian-barbecue":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/mongolian-barbecue","n":"Mongolian barbecue","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Taiwan cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Mongolian barbecue is a method of preparing stir-fried noodle dishes. Despite its name, the dish is not Mongolian, nor was it influenced by Mongolian cuisine. It was developed in Taiwan by a waishengren during the 1950s. Furthermore, it is also unrelated to actual barbecue traditions (such as American or Korean barbecue), since it is not cooked on a perforated grill above the smoke of an open flame, but rather a specialized flatiron grill. The kind of grill used to cook it is in the shape of a circle, and an upside-down wok was, in 1979, used to cook the dish in Taiwanese establishments. It has more in common with Teppanyaki."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-mongolian-barbecue"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongolian_barbecue"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Taiwan cuisine","cuisine/taiwan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Cooking in Chinglish","ref":"site/cookinginchinglish-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cookinginchinglish.com","note":"Taiwanese home recipes from Edwina, who grew up in Taiwan.","url":"https://cookinginchinglish.com","suggested":true},{"name":"Tiny Urban Kitchen: Taiwanese Recipes","ref":"site/tinyurbankitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"tinyurbankitchen.com","note":"Small set of Taiwanese recipes from Jen Che, a Taiwanese American blogger in Hong Kong.","url":"https://tinyurbankitchen.com/taiwanese-recipes/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Taiwan cuisine","links":[["886 (restaurant)","dish/886-restaurant"],["Ageh (food)","dish/ageh-food"],["Alivongvong","dish/alivongvong"],["Alkemē","dish/alkeme"],["Apple bread","dish/apple-bread"],["Bah-uân","dish/bah-uan"],["Braised pork rice",